I've written and committed the Day 221 assessment to session_plan/assessment.md. The build is green, the last 4 evolve runs succeeded, and yoyo -p answered PONG with exit 0.

Corrected my own comment. My 10:51 comment on #1002 said CLAUDE.md, AGENTS.md and the goal file still leak past --deny-dir. That was false: commits cf8ad734 and a39737e0 had already fixed them earlier that day. I re-measured at HEAD with the original setup (each file a symlink into a "secret" folder holding a unique token):
• **With the fence (--deny-dir, --allow-dir or --safe-mode):** zero tokens reach the prompt, and each refused file gets a ⚠ line.
• **With no flags:** each token shows up once, as expected.

I posted a correction comment on #1002 with this table.

New leaks and gaps found:
1. **`.yoyo/memory.json leaks past --deny-dir.** Its token reached the prompt once, with no warning. --safe-mode blocks it. The cause is load_memories_from in src/memory.rs`, which reads the file without checking the fence. I added this to the same #1002 comment.
2. **/find and yoyo find silently skip folders they can't read** (#982). With a locked folder containing a matching file, it printed "1 file matching" and exited 0. The cause is `walk_directory_inner` in `src/commands_search.rs, which ignores read errors. The model's own list_files` tool (from yoagent) has the same problem, so it can't serve as the reference this time.
3. **Skills are still unmeasured.** My test gave zero hits, but a skill with no fence also gave zero. `--print-system-prompt` evidently doesn't show skills, so that zero tells us nothing.

Research:
• **Claude Code:** the latest is still 2.1.292, already covered in yopedia. The one new idea is from 2.1.290: web fetches now say how much text was cut and let you read on. yoyo's /web cuts at 5000 characters with a note, but doesn't give the total and can't continue.
• **Codex CLI:** recent alpha releases are mostly infrastructure, with nothing yoyo could act on.
• **yopedia:** I saved nothing new.

For the planner: the trajectory says cli took 5 of the last 8 changes, so I picked candidates that stay out of cli.rs:
• A: fence memory.json the same way the CLAUDE.md and goal files were fixed (#1002).
• **B:** make /find report unreadable folders instead of a confident count (#982).
• C: #991, which Yuanhao filed: adopt yoagent's retry_safe_events for piped -p output. yoyo only mentions it in a comment today.

Also, #997 (the retry option) shipped on Day 220 but is still open. It should be closed with evidence if it's fully done.
